{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch1GoHm9gGjQ16Xx989nS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I found no P0 or P1 in this payload, and nothing here makes a declared condition false. The decision is GO; there are four P2 follow-ups.\n\n**What the payload is.** 15 new files under `.claude/hooks/_lib/`. They hold code moved out of three CLIs (`ceo-boot.py`, `check_contamination.py`, `context-budget.py`) for the PLAN-197 split, plus a new ceremony helper library (`_ceremony_toolkit`). I read each file against the entry point that loads it and against the installer.\n\n**Checks that came out clean**\n- **Name lookup after the move.**\n  - `ceo-boot.py:114-116` runs each part file inside its own namespace.\n  - `context-budget.py:199-203` rebinds functions and classes from the parts into its own namespace.\n  - `check_contamination.py:403-505` and `_contamination/__init__.py` do the same.\n  - Every outside name the moved code uses exists in the entry point once loading finishes. That includes `FileWalker`, the `_PERSONAL_PATH_*` constants, `PersonalPathUnreadable` and `_audit_emit`. Test patches on those names still take effect.\n  - `__file__` still resolves to the entry point, so `main()`'s default repository root is unchanged.\n  - The `personal_path_verdict` wrapper calls the real implementation, not itself.\n- **Fail direction.** The contamination gate still exits 2 when it cannot read its input. The ceo-boot telemetry and audit-emit wrappers still fail open.\n- **Delivery to adopters.**\n  - `install.sh:1520-1549` copies every `_lib` subdirectory except the test entries.\n  - The upgrade manifest delivers `.claude/hooks` as a whole directory.\n  - None of these packages is a registered hook, so a failure cannot block a session.\n- **Python.** Standard library only. Nothing breaks on 3.9: `tuple[...]` appears only in deferred annotations, and `Path.is_relative_to` exists from 3.9.\n- **Conditions.** Condition 7 (thin entry points over `_lib` modules) matches this code. Condition 5's 13 kernel lines rightly leave these packages out, because their entry points are not kernel.\n\n**P2 follow-ups**\n\n1. **The ceremony toolkit's default mode always refuses** — `.claude/hooks/_lib/_ceremony_toolkit/preflight.py:50-62`.\n   - `_canonical_patterns()` looks for a top-level `_CANONICAL_GUARDS = [...]` in `check_canonical_edit.py`.\n   - After the PLAN-197 split, that file only imports the list from `_lib/canonical_edit/guards.py`. The one remaining assignment is the empty fallback inside the `except` at `check_canonical_edit.py:124`.\n   - So any call without explicit `canonical_patterns` raises `canonical_guard_policy_unavailable`.\n   - It fails closed and nothing calls it yet. But the docstring says it reads \"the actual guard policy\", and every test passes explicit patterns, so the break went unnoticed.\n   - Fix: read `.claude/hooks/_lib/canonical_edit/guards.py`, refuse an empty list, and add a test of the default mode against the real tree.\n\n2. **The ceremony summary doesn't check that both results are about the same file** — `.claude/hooks/_lib/_ceremony_toolkit/bundle_builder.py:8-27`.\n   - `build_ceremony_summary` marks `ready_for_owner_review` true when the sentinel check passed and some signature check passed.\n   - A caller can pair a valid signature over one file with a scope check of a different sentinel and still get `ready_for_owner_review: True`.\n   - Fix: carry the checked file's path and sha256 in both results and require them to match.\n\n3. **A `_lib` module depends on the scripts folder being importable** — `.claude/hooks/_lib/_contamination/term_scan.py:12`.\n   - It imports `_contamination_inventory`, which lives in `.claude/scripts/`. That works only because running `check_contamination.py` puts its own folder on the import path.\n   - Loading the gate any other way fails at import, e.g. `runpy.run_path` or a spec loader from another folder.\n   - Fix: have the entry point add its own folder to `sys.path`, or pass `scan_rule_one` and `RuleOneInputError` in as arguments, as it already does for `FileWalker`.\n\n4. **Comments that now point at the wrong place.**\n   - `.claude/scripts/check_contamination.py:56` says \"See the RULE 2 block below\". That block now lives in `_lib/_contamination/personal_constants.py`.\n   - Some moved comments say \"two hundred lines up\", \"three lines up\" or \"the CENSUS above\" about code that is now in a different file. Examples: `personal_facade_io.py` (allowlist loader) and `personal_path_policy.py` (`_oserror_reason`, `_personal_path_reason_is_visible`).\n   - Fix: replace the relative positions with module or function names.\n\n**Noted, not a finding.** `_save_task_emit_state` in `telemetry_candidates.py` opens its `.tmp` file without refusing a symlink. That code moved over unchanged, so it is not a regression in this release."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4155,"cache_read_input_tokens":193245,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4155},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1aeb651e-484c-4168-99bd-f9adce0be74b","uuid":"0c3d4549-9aae-42c0-9b14-9e707fb641fb","timestamp":"2026-11-13T16:51:54.148Z","request_id":"req_011Ch1GoHTYin1UVt7hwv8Ce"}
