inel B gives ready_for_owner_review: True. Minimal fix: carry the checked file's path and sha256 in both results and require them to match in the summary.\\n3. P2 - .claude/hooks/_lib/_contamination/term_scan.py:12. A _lib module imports `_contamination_inventory`, which lives in .claude/scripts/. It resolves only because running check_contamination.py puts its own folder first on sys.path. Failure scenario: loading the gate through runpy.run_path or a spec loader from another folder fails at import with ModuleNotFoundError. Minimal fix: have the entry point add its own folder to sys.path, or pass scan_rule_one and RuleOneInputError in as arguments, as term_scan already does for FileWalker.\\n4. P2 - .claude/scripts/check_contamination.py:56 says 'See the RULE 2 block below', but that block now lives in _lib/_contamination/personal_constants.py. Some moved comments also give positions that no longer hold ('two hundred lines up', 'three lines up', 'the CENSUS above'), e.g. in personal_facade_io.py (allowlist loader) and personal_path_policy.py (_oserror_reason, _personal_path_reason_is_visible). Minimal fix: replace the relative positions with module or function names.\\n\\nNoted, not a finding: _save_task_emit_state in telemetry_candidates.py opens its .tmp file with O_CREAT|O_TRUNC and no O_NOFOLLOW. That code moved over unchanged, so it is not a regression in this delta.\",\"decision\":\"GO\",\"sentence\":\"The new _lib packages in this payload keep their entry points' name lookup, fail direction, stdlib-only and Python 3.9 rules, no declared condition is false against them, and the only defects found are four P2s in an unused ceremony library, one import-path dependency and stale comments.\"}","structured_output":{"report":"SCOPE OF PAYLOAD 7/32: 15 new files under .claude/hooks/_lib/ - _ceo_boot_parts/telemetry_candidates.py, _ceremony_toolkit/{__init__,bundle_builder,preflight}.py, _contamination/{__init__,cli_checks,personal_constants,personal_facade_io,person